{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/534013-requiem-information-so-far-on-paris-or-vienna","id":534013,"title":"Requiem information so far on Paris or Vienna","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-30T22:07:38-07:00","id":534013,"title":"Requiem information so far on Paris or Vienna","content":"I am running a crossover game taking place in the early 20th century <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465832-world-of-darkness-the-golden-eagle-actual-play\">AP Here</a> which jumps from location to location. The current story I am working on is Vienna, then Paris. I was wondering if anyone can point me to any information about those locations in the Requiem setting, be it NPCs, Bloodline activity, discussion of Covenant relations, history, etc. I am well capable of making things up, but if there is stuff out there that does not go against what I have written I would like to incorporate it.<br /> <br /> Thanks for any answers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T05:20:20-07:00","id":534215,"title":"","content":"Paris has a paragraph write-up in Damnation City. But it doesn't say much beyond the kindred breed successive generations of Parisian families.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1681-murder-of-crows","name":"Murder-of-Crows","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1681_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T09:35:43-07:00","id":534494,"title":"","content":"We also know from 2nd Edition that the Carthian Movement was born in the fires of revolutionary France, where Emmanuel Baptiste Carth, who was a pseudonym for another vampire, produced pamphlets that inspired the Movement. It spread like a virus from Paris to everywhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T11:09:50-07:00","id":534605,"title":"","content":"I would just like to mention that I'm highly interested in the answer to Samedi's questions as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T11:21:47-07:00","id":534617,"title":"","content":"Haven't found much official about my hometown Vienna in the books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T12:22:41-07:00","id":534702,"title":"","content":"The Nameless faction of Belial's Brood is found all over the globe, but is noted to be particularly strong in Calais, Edinburgh and Vienna. The Geheim bloodline has a history of rightful claiming of domains in Vienna and Prague, though with the waning of traditional aristocracy and their flubs with the Nazis they don't hold nearly as much sway as they did before. There is a belief among the Lancea Sanctum that the blade of their namesake lance is in Vienna.<br /> <br /> The Sangiovanni have been welcome to Paris since the close of the 19th century and the Duchagne bloodline was founded and remains centralized from there. The Architects of the Monolith operate out of Paris, led by Ermenjart la Charpenti\u00e8re, who seems quite insane, though they suffered drawbacks after a move against the Lancea Sanctum. The ancient Invictus House Machten, a nosferatu line, is based in the Parisian sewers, backing up the Invictus Prince of Paris with 'Gestapo-like tactics.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-31-2015, 03:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T13:00:46-07:00","id":534734,"title":"","content":"I have not acquired the pdf with the Geheim bloodline yet, but I am now considering it. When we hit the 30s and 40s the Nazis will be among the Antagonists (there is a Viennese Ivory Claw group who will be backing them) were the Geheim backers? I may could use them as antagonists with that.<br /> <br /> I have the Invictus and Lancea et Sanctum as having held power in Vienna for some time, but with the influx of more bohemian culture they weakened slightly and then after World War I their position has weakened more, as other covenants, especially Carthians, begin to establish themselves. This will become more established as a shadow war as the conflict between Fascists and Communists heats up the late 20s and into the 30s. This first visit is June 1920, and the Invictus and Lancea et Sanctum are trying to clamp down on their control. The only PC Kindred is a Russian Daeva Invictus. They should be back several times...as I say above a major WW oriented villain is based there.<br /> <br /> I clearly have a lot of reading to do before Paris <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I will have to track down the appropriate Bloodline Books. I have no specific plans for Paris politics yet, beyond Invictus needs to be able to move around without too much trouble given the PCs are based just outside the city right now, and will be until it falls.<br /> <br /> Thanks for all the answers so far! I may add cities to the thread as the campaign progresses heh. Seems better for research than to keep making new ones","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T13:10:51-07:00","id":534742,"title":"","content":"Lets see. They held salons devoted to esoterica, and it's rumored that they didn't restrict their invitations to Kindred, so there may have been other supernatural beings there. They declined in power after the Thirty Years' War, though still rich. They infiltrated a number of secret societies around that time, including the Thule Society, which they thought might help enhance their mystical strength. Members from it formed the Nazi party and while the Geheim <i>may</i> have had nothing to do with it the word was out that they were involved and it didn't help their already dwindling prestige.<br /> <br /> It looks like Paris is pretty firmly Invictus, in the book setting, at least. They likely have strong Lancea Sanctum supporters, but Paris also has a growing Carthian movement since socialist vampires joined up in the early 1900s.<br /> <br /> Since you mentioned Werewolf, there's also the Eigner Lodge and Clinic, which has been around in Vienna since the early 1900s as well. They take a Jungian approach to the dreams of werewolves, specifically the prophetic ones, and help a lot with dream interpretation. In the second edition book it suggests they help werewolves deal with the trauma of their First Change, as well.<br /> <br /> As a rambling and completely unrelated aside, considering how many mentions there are of Paris and Vienna and other major cities throughout cities in the vampire books, and how few are mentioned in the werewolf line, it's sort of disappointing. There's a stereotype that werewolves are 'stick to the country' savages and barbarians. Like during the Dark Eras Kickstarter, people were urging others not to vote for Viking Werewolf because it's 'too obvious.' And while it's certainly a valid stereotype in terms of most werewolf media, it doesn't really hold true with Werewolf the Forsaken, where werewolves are established as existing wherever people do, but there's still little mention of them in the cities. Even their dark era in New York seems to represent them at a time when the city itself is at its a particularly barbaric low. Fortunately it seems like second edition isn't sticking with the old stereotype.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-31-2015, 04:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T14:11:58-07:00","id":534801,"title":"","content":"Honestly I did not think about asking for city material for Werewolf on that forum, which I suppose only backs up your point. It's certainly not any issue with the folks over there. I had not given too much consideration to Werewolves in major cities* though for this game I had Vienna set up as tightly Pure (mostly Ivory Claw and Fire-Touched) who found control was slipping with the decline of the aristocracy. The Werewolf leg is dealing with infiltrating enemy territory in 1920 Vienna, and their control will slip until the back the Fascists then Nazis. I have a Werewolf set up in New Haven for my Geist campaign, but not set much up for Demon yet.<br /> <br /> I am sure I will find use for the Geheim. I tracked down their book. Thank you. I can deal with Paris as Invictus, especially given as I say an Invictus PC.<br /> <br /> I appreciate the continued information. Thanks!<br /> <br /> <br /> *well except that one I saw in London. His hair was perfect...I'd love to meet his tailor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T14:33:21-07:00","id":534817,"title":"","content":"I'd totally use Chris Allen's awesome stuff as a point of inspiration for werewolf in Paris.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T21:14:16-07:00","id":535186,"title":"","content":"Although Vienna isn't mentioned specifically, the Septimi bloodline are noted as being strongest in Germany and the former Austrian Empire, despite continued efforts by the Lancea et Sanctum to exterminate them. Most join the Carthian movement, and they usually keep a low profile anywhere that the Sanctified have any power, but they may preach their philosophy more openly in places where the Lance is weak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 06-01-2015, 12:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T21:52:52-07:00","id":535222,"title":"","content":"Giving the undermining of the Invictus and Lancea et Sanctum by Carthians is a major thing going on with the Kindred, I will look into this. Thank you Catdoom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness